    q("sql", "hard", ["retention"], "How would you compute monthly user retention with SQL?", "Assign each user a cohort month from their first activity, join to their later activity months, count distinct active users per cohort and month offset and divide by the cohort size.", ["Cohort month", "Month offset", "Active users over cohort size"], ["Why might retention numbers be misleading for new cohorts?"]),
    q("pandas", "medium", ["pandas"], "How do you detect and treat outliers in a numeric column and when should you keep them?", "Use summary statistics, box plots, the IQR rule or z-scores to find them, then investigate whether they are errors or real. Fix or remove errors, cap or transform genuine extremes if needed, and keep them when they carry the signal, such as fraud.", ["Detect with IQR or z-score", "Investigate the cause", "Keep real signal"], ["How do outliers affect different models?"]),
    q("python", "medium", ["python"], "How would you speed up a Python function that computes similarity between every pair of 10,000 vectors?", "Use NumPy matrix operations instead of loops, normalise vectors and use a matrix product for cosine similarity, process in blocks to limit memory and consider approximate nearest neighbour search if exact results are not needed.", ["Vectorise with matrix products", "Block processing", "Approximate search"], ["How much memory does the full matrix need?"]),
    q("ml", "easy", ["overfitting"], "What is the difference between parameters and hyperparameters, with an example of each?", "Parameters are learned from data, such as regression weights, while hyperparameters are set before training, such as the learning rate or tree depth, and tuned with validation.", ["Learned vs chosen", "Weights vs depth", "Tuned with validation data"], ["Which would you tune first for a random forest?"]),
    q("afiniti-scenario", "medium", ["modelling"], "Scenario: you are asked to predict which customers will call support again. What do you ask first and how do you start?", "Ask what action the prediction will drive and what window counts as again, check what data exists and when it is available, build a simple baseline with time-based validation and measure improvement against the current process.", ["Clarify the goal and definition", "Check data availability", "Baseline and time-based validation"], ["What would make the prediction unusable in practice?"], kind="scenario"),
